From: Chad Monroe <chad@monroe.io>
Date: Wed, 25 Mar 2026 21:01:17 -0700
Subject: [PATCH] wifi: mt76: guard airtime counters against overflow

The firmware airtime and channel MIB counters can report a delta that
is larger than the time between two polls. mac80211 then charges a
station for airtime that it did not use, and the survey reports more
busy time than elapsed time.

Clamp each channel MIB delta to the time since the previous poll plus
one jiffy, for the gap between the firmware sample and the jiffies
read. Clamp each station airtime delta to the time since the end of
the previous all-station report plus one request period, because the
delivery delay of a report varies. Keep the station counters as u64
per-AC values: the mt7915 firmware reports absolute counters, and the
mt7996 sums must not wrap. Clear the mt7915 WTBL counters from the MAC
work after BIT(30) is set, under the device mutex that the other WTBL
update users hold. Drop a pending clear when the driver frees a WTBL
index or does a full reset, so that the next owner keeps its counters.
Report the mt7996 per-link TX and RX durations as the sums of the
per-AC counters of the link.

Signed-off-by: Chad Monroe <chad@monroe.io>
